{"slug":"tokyo-xtreme-racer-3","title":"Tokyo Xtreme Racer 3","desc":"PS2, Genki 2003 (USA)","notes":["Genki games: the car models were decoded from scratch (the format has no public description).","Folder names are the number of the game's archive entry (no car names are known).  One car = the first (most detailed) of its levels of detail.","The car file is a tree of parts and holds EVERY variant of the shop (5 bodies, 5 front bumpers, several bonnets, wings ...); the variants of a part sit on the same place.  The car here is the stock set: the first variant of every part, each part at its place in the tree.  Moving parts (pop-up headlights) are in their closed position.  The game's hull / shadow volumes are left out.","Textures: the pictures of the game's body-part file (body, bumpers, grilles, lamps, decals); the cars of Racing Battle and Tokyo Xtreme Racer 3 come with the livery of the file, Kaido Racer / Drift with the plain white body picture (the game colours the car at run time).  Parts without a picture have the game's own material colour (black interior, tinted glass ...).","No wheels: they are separate models in the game.  The game's wheels are in the folder _Rims (most detailed version only).","Left out on purpose: stickers and number plates that the game textures at run time (blank white cards), light-glow sprites and reflection layers (Kaido Racer 1 / 2, Drift), the 4 cards behind the wheels of Kaido Racer 1.","The game's triangle strips run on from one piece to another without a break.  Racing Battle C1 GP and Kaido Racer 2 mark the joins in the vertex data (see below); Kaido Racer 1, Drift and TXR3 do not, there the converter removes a join when the two triangles around a long edge do not form a flat quad with continuous normals, or when a long triangle contradicts the normals of its corners (real long slivers such as door sills and roof bands are kept).","Every car is there twice: the odd entry (e.g. 00209) is the full model, the next even entry (00210) is the same car as the game uses it in a race (the first level of detail of its LOD folder, a little less detailed).  The livery of the file is the same."],"tags":["tokyo-xtreme-racer-3"],"sections":[{"key":"cars","label":"Cars","items":[["00137","",422659,"tokyo-xtreme-racer-3","car-00137.zip","thumbs/tokyo-xtreme-racer-3/cars/car-00137.webp"],["00138","",353107,"tokyo-xtreme-racer-3","car-00138.zip","thumbs/tokyo-xtreme-racer-3/cars/car-00138.webp"],["00139","",325484,"tokyo-xtreme-racer-3","car-00139.zip","thumbs/tokyo-xtreme-racer-3/cars/car-00139.webp"],["00140","",302431,"tokyo-xtreme-racer-3","car-00140.zip","thumbs/tokyo-xtreme-racer-3/cars/car-00140.webp"],["00141","",283078,"tokyo-xtreme-racer-3","car-00141.zip","thumbs/tokyo-xtreme-racer-3/cars/car-00141.webp"],["00142","",264776,"tokyo-xtreme-racer-3","car-00142.zip","thumbs/tokyo-xtreme-racer-3/cars/car-00142.webp"],["00143","",461533,"tokyo-xtreme-racer-3","car-00143.zip","thumbs/tokyo-xtreme-racer-3/cars/car-00143.webp"],["00144","",368274,"tokyo-xtreme-racer-3","car-00144.zip","thumbs/tokyo-xtreme-racer-3/cars/car-00144.webp"],["00145","",329923,"tokyo-xtreme-racer-3","car-00145.zip","thumbs/tokyo-xtreme-racer-3/cars/car-00145.webp"],["00146","",329102,"tokyo-xtreme-racer-3","car-00146.zip","thumbs/tokyo-xtreme-racer-3/cars/car-00146.webp"],["00147","",299734,"tokyo-xtreme-racer-3","car-00147.zip","thumbs/tokyo-xtreme-racer-3/cars/car-00147.webp"],["00148","",299125,"tokyo-xtreme-racer-3","car-00148.zip","thumbs/tokyo-xtreme-racer-3/cars/car-00148.webp"],["00149","",425364,"tokyo-xtreme-racer-3","car-00149.zip","thumbs/tokyo-xtreme-racer-3/cars/car-00149.webp"],["00150","",333207,"tokyo-xtreme-racer-3","car-00150.zip","thumbs/tokyo-xtreme-racer-3/cars/car-00150.webp"],["00151","",431022,"tokyo-xtreme-racer-3","car-00151.zip","thumbs/tokyo-xtreme-racer-3/cars/car-00151.webp"],["00152","",339129,"tokyo-xtreme-racer-3","car-00152.zip","thumbs/tokyo-xtreme-racer-3/cars/car-00152.webp"],["00153","",3